# fixedbugs, defect 562, lane b18-ffi, 2026-10-10 (panel 202's R2; the
# ffi-pragmatist's `c99`).
#
# The header defines `twice` with `inline` alone, which in C provides no
# external definition, and nothing else defines it. Until 2026-10-10 `build`
# told *the linker cannot find `twice`, and no group in this program says
# which library has it*, false of a header that defines it, and `run`, at
# `-O2`, inlined the call and printed 6: two verdicts. Each module's unit
# now references what it calls at every level, so both refuse it, told what
# C wants and the two ways out.

extern "fixedbugs-562-inline.h"
    function twice(x: i64) -> i64  #~ ffi_missing_link

function main()
    print(twice(x: 3))
